    "primary_question": "What should CHAMPVA beneficiaries, families, caregivers, and providers know about eligibility, enrollment, finding care, costs, claims, pharmacy benefits, and appeals?",
    "summary": "Source-backed CHAMPVA guidance for beneficiaries, families, caregivers, and providers, covering eligibility, enrollment, care access, costs, other insurance, claims, pharmacy benefits, and decision reviews.",
    "body_markdown": "\n## Start here\n\nCHAMPVA Resources is ValorWell's source-backed guide library for the Civilian Health and Medical Program of the Department of Veterans Affairs.\n\nUse this hub to find practical explanations of:\n\n- who may qualify for CHAMPVA and how eligibility changes after major life events;\n- how to apply, update enrollment information, and understand CHAMPVA identification;\n- how authorized non-VA care, VA CHAMPVA In-House Treatment Initiative (CITI) care, and pharmacy benefits work;\n- provider participation, assignment, allowable amounts, deductibles, cost sharing, and the catastrophic cap;\n- how CHAMPVA coordinates with Medicare and other health insurance;\n- how to file, correct, and track claims; and\n- how decision reviews and appeals work when VA makes a CHAMPVA determination.\n\nThe articles in this section use current VA guidance, regulations, forms, and other primary sources whenever available. Operational details can change, so pages with phone numbers, addresses, forms, payer information, pharmacy routing, or other time-sensitive instructions are rechecked against current official sources.\n\n*Last researched: September 19, 2026.*\n",
