    "slug": "va-community-care",
    "title": "VA Community Care Resources",
    "primary_question": "What should Veterans and community providers know about VA Community Care eligibility, referrals, authorizations, scheduling, the Community Care Network, billing, and care coordination?",
    "summary": "Source-backed guidance on the Veterans Community Care Program, including eligibility and access standards, referrals and authorizations, the Community Care Network, scheduling, continued care, provider arrangements, billing, and related care-coordination issues.",
    "body_markdown": "\n## About this category\n\nVA Community Care is the system VA uses to arrange eligible care from community providers when applicable requirements are met. The **Veterans Community Care Program** determines when covered Veterans may receive VA-authorized care in the community, while the **Community Care Network (CCN)** is VA's main contracted network for delivering much of that authorized care.\n\nUse the articles in this category to understand:\n\n- how Community Care eligibility and access standards work;\n- the difference between the Veterans Community Care Program and CCN;\n- how referrals, authorizations, scheduling, and continued-care requests work;\n- how VA uses CCN, Veterans Care Agreements, and other provider arrangements;\n- what an authorization covers and how an episode of care is defined;\n- provider billing and claims rules;\n- prescriptions and other care-coordination issues; and\n- what to do when a Community Care process stalls or the information you receive conflicts.\n\nThese resources are educational and are designed to separate rules that are often discussed as though they are the same. Eligibility, referral, authorization, network participation, scheduling, coverage, and payment are distinct questions.\n\nOperational details can change. For a specific referral, authorization, appointment, or claim, confirm the current status with VA and, when applicable, the Community Care Network administrator.\n\n*Last researched: September 25, 2026.*\n",
    "faq": [],
